      bearCase: "The bearish outlook is driven by persistent regulatory uncertainty and fragmentation, as exemplified by Ireland\'s exclusion of crypto from tax-advantaged accounts. This could deter mainstream adoption, particularly among risk-averse investors seeking tax efficiencies. Macroeconomic headwinds, such as persistently high inflation and rising interest rates, could also continue to pressure risk assets like cryptocurrencies, leading to sustained volatility and potential capital outflows.",
      neutralCase: "A neutral perspective suggests that the crypto market will continue to experience a push-pull dynamic between regulatory restrictions and expanding market access. While some regions will adopt cautious approaches, others will embrace integration. Bitcoin and other major cryptocurrencies will likely remain sensitive to global macroeconomic conditions, but their fundamental technology and growing user base will provide a floor for long-term value, leading to sideways or range-bound price action in the medium term.",
      probabilityWeightedOutlook: "Our probability-weighted outlook suggests a \'Neutral to Moderately Bullish\' trajectory for the broader crypto market. We assign a 40% probability to a neutral case, 40% to a bullish case (driven by adoption and clarity), and 20% to a bearish case (driven by regulatory clampdowns and macro pressures). The net effect is a slow but steady path towards greater integration, albeit with regional disparities and intermittent volatility.",
      potentialCatalysts: ["Further regulatory clarity in major economies (e.g., EU MiCA implementation, US legislation).", "Increased institutional investment and product offerings (e.g., spot Bitcoin ETFs in more regions).", "Significant technological advancements or widespread adoption of blockchain applications.", "A shift in global macroeconomic sentiment towards risk-on assets."],
